# Apple fetches the app-site-association file and expects JSON. It has no file
# extension, so set the type explicitly rather than letting it default to
# application/octet-stream. Only /i/* and /e/* are claimed as universal links
# (see the file itself); the home, privacy, and support pages stay web pages.
/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
  Content-Type: application/json

# SL-H-035 — a baseline security posture for a static site. The named risk is
# clickjacking and XSS amplification "if pages grow scripts", so the two directives
# doing the real work are `frame-ancestors 'none'` and a default of `'none'`.
#
# THE ONE THAT WOULD BREAK EVERYTHING IF DROPPED: connect-src names
# firestore.googleapis.com. The invite landing page reads
# groupInvitePreviews/{inviteId} straight from the REST API — there is no server
# here, so that fetch IS the feature. A CSP without it turns every invite link into
# the "invalid invite" state, silently, with a console error no visitor will see.
# `test/route.test.mjs` pins it for that reason.
#
# 'unsafe-inline' IS PRESENT AND IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT. The page's script and styles
# are inline by design — no build step, no bundler, nothing to cache-bust. Hashes
# would be stricter and would break on every copy edit, silently, because a blocked
# inline script leaves the page looking merely empty. For a static page with no user
# input and no third-party script, the honest trade is: keep inline, deny everything
# else, and make framing impossible.
#
# HSTS carries no `preload`. The directive is cheap to add and the PRELOAD LIST is a
# one-way door — removal takes months and it applies to every subdomain of
# searchlight.social. That is a founder decision, not a header default.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src https://firestore.googleapis.com; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
